@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Key Azure DevOps Services";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Azure DevOps provides a suite of cloud-based services that help teams manage software development, automate workflows, and deploy applications efficiently.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-4">
        <p>
            Microsoft Azure DevOps offers a set of core services designed to support the **entire software development lifecycle (SDLC)**. These services integrate seamlessly to provide **version control, build automation, testing, project tracking, and artifact management**, making DevOps adoption easier and more efficient.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Core Services of Azure DevOps</h2>
        <p>Azure DevOps consists of the following key services:</p>
        
        <div class="row align-items-center">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Azure Boards</h4>
                <p>Azure Boards provides **agile project management** with features such as Kanban boards, Scrum boards, dashboards, and reporting tools. It helps teams track work items, plan sprints, and visualize project progress.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="~/css/Images/AzureDevOps/Azure Boards.png" alt="Azure Boards" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Boards enables efficient agile project management.</small></p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/repos/media/azure-repos.png" alt="Azure Repos" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Repos provides cloud-based Git repositories.</small></p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Azure Repos</h4>
                <p>Azure Repos offers **cloud-hosted Git repositories** for source control management. It supports branching, pull requests, code reviews, and collaboration with other team members. Developers can integrate with GitHub or Bitbucket for enhanced version control.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Azure Pipelines</h4>
                <p>Azure Pipelines provides **CI/CD automation** to build, test, and deploy applications across different environments. It supports multiple programming languages and deployment targets, including containers, virtual machines, and Kubernetes.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/media/azure-pipelines.png" alt="Azure Pipelines" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Pipelines automates builds, testing, and deployments.</small></p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/test-plans/media/azure-test-plans.png" alt="Azure Test Plans" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Test Plans help ensure software quality with manual and automated testing.</small></p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Azure Test Plans</h4>
                <p>Azure Test Plans is a **test management solution** that allows teams to run manual and automated tests. It helps track test coverage, log defects, and ensure software quality through integrated reporting and tracking.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Azure Artifacts</h4>
                <p>Azure Artifacts enables **package management** for storing, sharing, and managing dependencies across teams. It supports popular package formats like NuGet, npm, Maven, and Python.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/artifacts/media/azure-artifacts.png" alt="Azure Artifacts" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Artifacts stores and manages project dependencies.</small></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Azure DevOps provides a **comprehensive suite of tools** for managing software development, version control, automation, and quality assurance. Each service plays a crucial role in streamlining DevOps workflows and enhancing team collaboration.
        </p>
        <p>
            By leveraging **Azure Boards, Repos, Pipelines, Test Plans, and Artifacts**, teams can ensure an efficient, high-quality, and scalable software development process.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-start mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("WhatIsAzureDevOps", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: What is Azure DevOps?</a>
    </div>
</div>